China Playbook — Trade data 2025 update and the price-per-kg test (13 Oct 2026)

Source: UN Comtrade public API (comtradeapi.un.org/public/v1/preview), imports, HS 6-digit, reporters India (699), Indonesia (360), Thailand (764), Malaysia (458). Filters: partner2Code 0, motCode 0, customsCode C00. "Established" = Japan, Korea, US, Germany, Austria, Italy, France, UK, Switzerland, Sweden, Finland, Poland, Netherlands, Belgium, Spain, Denmark, Czechia. Price per kg only for Indonesia and Thailand (India and Malaysia weights are estimated). Import data shows country of origin, not brand, and leaves out machines built locally (e.g. Komatsu and SANY in Indonesia, almost all construction equipment in India). Script: an3.py in session scratchpad.

1. Did the gains last into 2025?

Mostly yes. 43 product markets over US$20m in 2025:

China's share rose more than 2 points in 25, held within 2 points in 6, fell more than 2 points in 12.
China had half or more of imports in 6 markets in 2019, 19 in 2024 and 24 in 2025.
China's 2025 share was above its 2019 share in 40 of 43.
7 of the 12 falls were in India: injection moulding 53→47%, lasers 47→44%, compressors 53→49%, machining centres 15→12%, off-road trucks 43→39%, cranes (842619) 61→55%, crane trucks (842641) 90→87%. These line up with the duties and local plants (Ch 5). India is the one market where the shift paused in 2025.
